  "answer": "The goal was not met. Only 2 of the 5 cases were confirmed, each on its own scene. On 023b7fcc, cars running 1 s late at 1.5x speed (S1) made every run fail. On 096988dd, cars running 1 s early at 0.75x speed (S5) also made every run fail. Almost every failure has the same cause: the policy drifts left out of its lane into a car in the next lane, often while driving well below traffic speed, and even when the route command says RIGHT or STRAIGHT. So the retiming mostly decides whether a car is alongside when the drift happens, rather than creating a hard cut-in. The best third candidate is 19f339ba at -0.5 s and 1.5x (S18). It failed in more than half its runs, but its range still reaches below one half, and several of its side hits were cars coming from behind where the policy's fault is unclear. No failure counts are flagged as possible simulator artifacts.",
